==Icelandic==
{{wikipedia|lang=is}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|drykkr||a drink|lang=non}} from the {{proto|Germanic|drunkiz|lang=is}}, whence also Old English {{term|drync|lang=ang}} and Old High German {{term|trunch}}. Cognate with the Danish {{term|drink|lang=da}} and Swedish {{term|dryck|lang=sv}}.

===Noun===
{{is-noun|m|drykkjar|drykkir}}

# a [[drink]], a [[beverage]]; {{gloss|a served beverage}}
# an [[alcoholic]] [[drink]]; {{gloss|a served alcoholic beverage}}

